.TH "LSMOD" "8" "2025-03-28" "kmod" "lsmod"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
lsmod - Show the status of modules in the Linux Kernel
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBlsmod\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBlsmod\fR is a trivial program which nicely formats the contents of the
\fI/proc/modules\fR, showing what kernel modules are currently loaded.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-s\fR, \fB--syslog\fR
.RS 4
Send errors to syslog instead of standard error.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-v\fR, \fB--verbose\fR
.RS 4
Print messages about what the program is doing.\& Usually \fBlsmod\fR prints
messages only if something goes wrong.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-V\fR, \fB--version\fR
.RS 4
Show version of program and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
.RS 4
Print the help message and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
